{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781147808759,"sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e9xNZOsU88s8p3lJYPN7LIo3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Selection Rules\n2: \n3: Effective date: 2026-05-08\n4: \n5: ## Source Reliability\n6: \n7: - When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n8: - Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n9: - The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n10: \n11: ## First-Wave Requirements\n12: \n13: Select exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n14: \n15: - Region is `North`.\n16: - Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n17: - Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n18: - The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n19: - Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n20: - Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.\n21: \n22: ## Selection Preference\n23: \n24: - Include the donor continuity anchor if it is eligible.\n25: - If more than three clinics are eligible, choose the anchor plus the lowest-cost eligible clinics.\n26: - If fewer than three clinics are eligible, choose only eligible clinics and flag the gap instead of relaxing hard requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Selection Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-08\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- When two files disagree about the same clinic eligibility field, use the newest dated source for that field.\n- Files titled or labeled as archived, future wave, or optional add-ons are planning context only. They do not override current first-wave selection rules.\n- The clinic roster gives baseline information, but newer storage updates control storage status where they conflict.\n\n## First-Wave Requirements\n\nSelect exactly three clinics. A selected clinic must satisfy all of these requirements:\n\n- Region is `North`.\n- Clinic status is `open` for the 2026-06-10 to 2026-06-14 launch window.\n- Effective storage status is accepted for first-wave use. Accepted statuses are `certified` and `certified after mitigation complete`. Not accepted: `expired`, `suspended`, `conditional pass pending`, or any status awaiting repair.\n- The named coordinator is available for the full launch window.\n- Transport delivery is no later than 2026-06-07.\n- Selected-clinic total rollout cost stays within the first-wave budget in `07_budget_and_costs.md`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/01_selection_rules.md","time":{"start":1781147808703,"end":1781147808758}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f0971e8486c9d81016a2a28a0c7348191819452765453e644"}},"id":"prt_eb4aeb3b30012hGBoGDpAsqcqU","sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","messageID":"msg_eb4ae7db2001j0nnslwxLRFtLJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781147808765,"sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_55RUNj84qY1e41kuoEuUEDcv","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/source_resolution.md`\n6: \n7: Record which sources control the first-wave clinic decision when files conflict or distract from the current rollout.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - The source reliability rule from `01_selection_rules.md`.\n12: - A note that `04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md` is newer than `02_site_roster.csv` and `03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv` for storage-status conflicts.\n13: - The effective storage status and source used for every clinic in `02_site_roster.csv`.\n14: - A note that archived policy excerpts, future-wave requests, and optional add-ons do not override the current first-wave selection rules.\n15: \n16: ## `answer/clinic_screen.md`\n17: \n18: Screen every clinic against the first-wave requirements.\n19: \n20: Required facts:\n21: \n22: - One row or entry for every clinic in `02_site_roster.csv`.\n23: - For each clinic: effective storage status, coordinator full-window availability, transport delivery date, total rollout cost if otherwise eligible, eligible `yes` or `no`, and the blocking reason when ineligible.\n24: - The current first-wave budget.\n25: - The selected-clinic total cost calculation.\n26: \n27: ## `answer/launch_recommendation.md`\n28: \n29: Write the final recommendation for the rollout coordinator.\n30: \n31: Required facts:\n32: \n33: - The three selected clinics.\n34: - Total rollout cost and remaining budget.\n35: - The anchor clinic and donor continuity code from the intake brief.\n36: - The carrier and delivery date for each selected clinic.\n37: - Short rejected-clinic summary.\n38: \n39: Rules:\n40: \n41: - Use local files only.\n42: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n43: - Use dollar amounts rounded to whole dollars unless a source provides cents.\n44: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n\n(End of file - total 44 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/source_resolution.md`\n\nRecord which sources control the first-wave clinic decision when files conflict or distract from the current rollout.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The source reliability rule from `01_selection_rules.md`.\n- A note that `04_storage_update_2026-05-06.md` is newer than `02_site_roster.csv` and `03_storage_audit_2026-04-18.csv` for storage-status conflicts.\n- The effective storage status and source used for every clinic in `02_site_roster.csv`.\n- A note that archived policy excerpts, future-wave requests, and optional add-ons do not override the current first-wave selection rules.\n\n## `answer/clinic_screen.md`\n\nScreen every clinic against the first-wave requirements.\n\nRequired facts:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781147808688,"end":1781147808760}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f0971e8486c9d81016a2a28a0c724819180493cfefb20f116"}},"id":"prt_eb4aeb3a40017SmaqJ8eDBOT3E","sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","messageID":"msg_eb4ae7db2001j0nnslwxLRFtLJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781147808765,"sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4qkxrTVHXplt6388YPEzXHQI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Budget And Cost Notes\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-05-08\n4: \n5: The first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n6: \n7: Use `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n8: \n9: The budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Budget And Cost Notes\n\nDate: 2026-05-08\n\nThe first-wave budget is `$20,000` for setup costs plus required transport costs.\n\nUse `setup_cost` from `02_site_roster.csv` and `transport_cost` from `06_transport_quotes.csv` to calculate each clinic's rollout cost. Optional add-ons, future-wave requests, and staff celebration supplies are not part of the first-wave budget.\n\nThe budget owner wants the recommendation to show the selected-clinic total and the remaining budget.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/07_budget_and_costs.md","time":{"start":1781147808722,"end":1781147808761}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f0971e8486c9d81016a2a28a0c7448191b1f34469ea6f080a"}},"id":"prt_eb4aeb3c90017K960QMfX8OnRv","sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","messageID":"msg_eb4ae7db2001j0nnslwxLRFtLJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781147808765,"sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_wWzv0vYROMKeKajbmB6E1ce6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/00_intake_brief.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/00_intake_brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Intake Brief\n2: \n3: Date: 2026-05-09\n4: \n5: The first-wave medication cooler rollout needs a short recommendation packet for the operations coordinator. The packet should select exactly three North-region clinics that can receive cooler kits before the June launch window.\n6: \n7: Keep this continuity fact with the final recommendation: Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor if it remains eligible, and its donor continuity code is `MJ-14`. The code was printed on already-approved training inserts and is not repeated in the later operations files.\n8: \n9: The launch window is 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14. All selected clinics need coordinator coverage for the full window and delivery no later than 2026-06-07.\n10: \n11: Do not include a separate narrative for future-wave clinic requests unless they change current first-wave eligibility.\n\n(End of file - total 11 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Intake Brief\n\nDate: 2026-05-09\n\nThe first-wave medication cooler rollout needs a short recommendation packet for the operations coordinator. The packet should select exactly three North-region clinics that can receive cooler kits before the June launch window.\n\nKeep this continuity fact with the final recommendation: Maple Junction Clinic is the donor continuity anchor if it remains eligible, and its donor continuity code is `MJ-14`. The code was printed on already-approved training inserts and is not repeated in the later operations files.\n\nThe launch window is 2026-06-10 through 2026-06-14. All selected clinics need coordinator coverage for the full window and delivery no later than 2026-06-07.\n\nDo not include a separate narrative for future-wave clinic requests unless they change current first-wave eligibility.","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tasks/clinic_rollout_plan/00_intake_brief.md","time":{"start":1781147808711,"end":1781147808764}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f0971e8486c9d81016a2a28a0c73c81918f43118d138d9a14"}},"id":"prt_eb4aeb3c1001Yin6BWF9YUijrB","sessionID":"ses_14b51bbdfffeviqUpVPyla3hD8","messageID":"msg_eb4ae7db2001j0nnslwxLRFtLJ"}}
